                    insight_won:            `Framework agreement in reach: you won the bid on margin, with client-fit and learner-relevance both strong. You translated a contradictory brief into a fundable objective and held the floor without gutting the deliverable — exactly the craft that turns one contract into a multi-year account.`,
                    insight_breach:         `You breached the 20% floor. Even a beautiful design at sub-floor margin sets a precedent that erodes the P&L and the unit's negotiating position — and the school will not sign it. Re-examine where cost leaked: bespoke-everything, an on-the-spot discount, or pricing full capacity.`,
                    insight_lost:           `The bid went to a competitor. With fit, relevance and margin not aligned, the panel saw either a generic programme at a custom price or an over-margin proposal. Re-examine the stakeholder you under-served and the lever that thinned the deliverable.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You won, but thin. The margin holds and the panel signed, yet fit or relevance is fragile — the programme is vulnerable on delivery and the framework agreement is not secured.`,
                    insight_relevance:      `Learner-relevance stayed low: the 120 time-poor managers will rate a theory-heavy journey poorly, the COO will see the scores, and there is no Cohort 2. The survey was your relevance input, not a slide.`,
                    insight_fit:            `Client-fit stayed low: the COO or HR did not see their outcome in the design. A custom programme that doesn't visibly serve the buyer's need reads as generic — and loses to the boutique.`,
                    insight_durable:        `You cleared the floor with a couple of points of headroom and kept fit strong — a margin solve that protected the deliverable rather than mutilating it. That is the difference between a profitable account and a Pyrrhic win.`,
                    insight_repeat:         `Two-thirds of Alpina's revenue is repeat business. A well-scoped, on-margin, relevant programme delivered to this standard is what converts a single €480k contract into a multi-year framework agreement.`,

                    hint_designover:        `You overspent the €90k design envelope — the overrun is bleeding into the delivery ceiling. In the mix/margin round you'll need extra savings just to get back to where targeted bespoke would have started.`,
                    hint_margin:            `You're still below the 20% floor (cost above €384k). The school won't sign a sub-floor bid. Find a cost lever that protects the deliverable — a bespoke→open swap plus core-faculty self-delivery.`,
                    hint_relevance:         `Learner-relevance is weak — the manager survey isn't shaping the design. Treat it as a design input and fund the coaching that converts frameworks into changed behaviour.`,
                    hint_fit:               `Client-fit is weak — the buyer can't see their outcome. Anchor the objective on the COO's measurable impact and build bespoke content where fit actually pays.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — fit and relevance healthy and you're on margin. Now price the 90-seat guarantee and defend the mix on value so the win survives contact with the panel.`,

